# Public orrery app vhost — ROUTING OWNED BY THIS REPO.
#
# The shared Caddy EDGE ENGINE (install, systemd unit, base Caddyfile, firewall,
# the deploy@ `systemctl reload|restart caddy` sudoers grant) is owned by podcast_scraper
# (ADR-114). The base Caddyfile does `import /etc/caddy/sites/*.caddy`, so this
# tenant vhost is picked up automatically once dropped in. ops/deploy_caddy_vhosts.sh
# installs it into /etc/caddy/sites/orrery.caddy, `caddy adapt`-gates the merged
# config, then `sudo -n systemctl reload caddy`.
#
# Domain: www.orrerylearn.com only. The apex orrerylearn.com is redirected to www by the
# Cloudflare zone itself (including /.well-known/acme-challenge/), so no apex request
# reaches the box and Caddy could never renew an apex cert (http-01 lands on www,
# tls-alpn-01 can't pass the proxy). Listing the apex here only made Caddy retry ACME
# hourly. If the Cloudflare redirect is ever removed, add the apex back with a
# `redir https://www.orrerylearn.com{uri}` block. Upstream is orrery's own nginx
# container on the reserved loopback port 8090 (ADR-114 §port map).
#
# Rollback: `rm /etc/caddy/sites/orrery.caddy && sudo systemctl reload caddy` —
# frees the vhost, nothing shared changes, the box stays up.
www.orrerylearn.com {
	import hardened
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8090
}
